  "pr_number": 341,
  "issue_number": 210,
  "issue_title": "[M1.17] Formalize and test the DEFER to human-review TTL expiry path under NATS partition",
  "issue_body": "**Summary:** What happens if the dashboard can't reach NATS to approve/deny a DEFER'd decision before its TTL expires?\n\n**Why:** DEFER is one of the Kernel's four decision types (ALLOW/TRANSFORM/DENY/DEFER); its expiry behavior under a network partition is safety-relevant and currently untested.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n- [ ] Document the intended behavior on TTL expiry (should default to DENY, per fail-closed)\n- [ ] Add a test simulating a NATS partition between dashboard and Kernel during a DEFER window\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-16T08:34:32.000Z",
